      "message": "feat(post): one NC file per operation\n\nA post option \"Output\", next to the Post picker: \"One program\" (the\ndefault - the combined program is byte-identical, every golden stays)\nor \"One file per operation\", which writes each program operation as\nits own standalone program into a folder.\n\n- Files are <program>_<nn>_<op>.<ext>: the project's stem (program\n  when unsaved), nn in program order, names cut to portable\n  characters; the extension is the script's own manifest entry.\n- Each op's own stream (posting::op_streams, the pieces the combined\n  stream is joined from) posts alone, so each file has the dialect's\n  header and units, its own tool change, the safe start (G90, work\n  offset, cancels, spindle and coolant for that op) and its own end\n  (coolant off, M5, home, M30). Suppressed ops write no file.\n- O-numbers: the engine publishes programNumber before onOpen (1 for a\n  whole job); Fanuc, Mazak and Fanuc Lathe write O0001, O0002... per\n  file.\n- One refusal refuses all: the program gate runs once, every op's post\n  must come back warning-free, and only then are the files written -\n  to a scratch folder in the target, then renamed into place.\n- PostOptions gains per_op, switched by the undoable SetPostOptions;\n  saved as a top-level per_op_files key written only when on.\n- UI: the Post action asks for a folder when per-op is chosen.\n\nFixes #111\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
